  "verbalization": "Cefamandole, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is linked to Urinary Tract Infection (UTI) through a chain of indications. The evidence suggests that Cefamandole is used to treat Escherichia Coli Infection, which in turn is associated with UTI. This implies a potential mechanism where Cefamandole may target bacterial pathogens that cause UTIs, such as Escherichia Coli, thereby contributing to the development of UTIs. The indirect pathway through Aztreonam and Clavulanic Acid further supports this relationship, as these antibiotics are often used in combination with Cefamandole to enhance抗菌 activity against UTI-causing bacteria. The cumulative evidence suggests that Cefamandole may play a role in the treatment or prevention of UTIs by targeting the bacterial pathogens that contribute to their development.",
